# Cursor indexing / Agent context — keep harness signal, drop bulk copies & runtime noise.
# Edit if you need to @-mention an ignored path intentionally.
# A path listed here is also blocked for the agent's file tools (Read, Write,
# Grep): do not add a path an agent must read or write, such as the session
# scratch directory (.scratch/) or its *.log and *.tmp files.
# Detail: reference/tool-ops-cursor.md "Ignore files and agent file tools".

# Harvested exports (very large; RFC copies and session dumps)
harvesting/

# Claude worktree duplicates
.claude/worktrees/

# Runtime harness data (regenerated; not source of truth in git)
.aitools/scratch/
.aitools/sessions/
.aitools/harness.db
.aitools/harness.db-shm
.aitools/harness.db-wal

# Huge channel artifacts — relay.md stays available; full sessions are for intentional deep reads
.aitools/channel/*-full-session.md
.aitools/channel/pre-failure-mode/

# Python envs and caches
**/__pycache__/
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/ENV/

# Stray file named nul
nul
